<i>at the Colobane bus stop,</i>

759
00:48:52,867 --> 00:48:54,401
<i>in front of the hospital.</i>

760
00:48:55,870 --> 00:48:56,970
<i>You can't miss him.</i>

761
00:48:59,039 --> 00:49:01,141
<i>I'll be monitoring</i>
<i>your progress.</i>

762
00:49:01,876 --> 00:49:05,613
<i>And... try to have a good time.</i>

763
00:49:05,680 --> 00:49:07,615
[ominous music]

764
00:49:27,602 --> 00:49:29,537
[ominous music continues]

765
00:49:36,778 --> 00:49:38,145
[One] What did he send you?

766
00:49:44,552 --> 00:49:45,352
[Two] It's done.

767
00:49:47,054 --> 00:49:48,155
<i>Are you okay?</i>

768
00:49:49,891 --> 00:49:51,191
[Two] I got fucked over.

769
00:49:52,760 --> 00:49:53,728
Is she okay?

770
00:49:54,829 --> 00:49:56,129
[India] <i>Momo is on it.</i>

771
00:49:56,196 --> 00:49:58,566
<i>Your papers will be ready</i>
<i>in three days.</i>

772
00:50:00,167 --> 00:50:01,368
[India] <i>See you in Dakar.</i>

773
00:50:06,139 --> 00:50:08,108
[Two] You're the only thing
I have left.

774
00:50:08,710 --> 00:50:09,744
[beeps]

775
00:50:11,411 --> 00:50:13,347
[pensive music]

776
00:50:33,400 --> 00:50:35,269
[crow caws]

777
00:50:43,778 --> 00:50:47,281
[cell phone chimes]

778
00:50:49,383 --> 00:50:51,986
He sent me the fucking address
where all my money is.

779
00:50:52,052 --> 00:50:53,220
That's what he sent me.

780
00:51:05,700 --> 00:51:07,467
[engine revs]

781
00:51:26,821 --> 00:51:28,155
[Two] What's he got on you?

782
00:51:32,794 --> 00:51:33,828
I met a woman here...

783
00:51:35,162 --> 00:51:36,831
18 years ago on a business trip.

784
00:51:39,701 --> 00:51:41,636
[melancholy music]

785
00:52:01,923 --> 00:52:03,190
She died two weeks ago.

786
00:52:06,794 --> 00:52:08,863
That's when I found out
I have a daughter here.

787
00:52:11,164 --> 00:52:12,867
[timer ticking]

788
00:52:17,471 --> 00:52:18,405
[beeps]

789
00:52:19,674 --> 00:52:21,308
[line rings]

790
00:52:22,142 --> 00:52:25,513
[cell phone ringing]

791
00:52:37,091 --> 00:52:38,492
She'd be 17, I think.

792
00:52:45,165 --> 00:52:46,166
I've never met her.

793
00:52:47,167 --> 00:52:48,736
I searched the internet
for her, but...

794
00:52:50,772 --> 00:52:52,840
all I have is a memorized
phone number.

795
00:52:57,210 --> 00:52:58,378
He knows who she is.

796
00:53:02,950 --> 00:53:04,118
[One] That's what he sent me.

797
00:53:04,184 --> 00:53:06,253
[cell phone chimes]

798
00:53:16,698 --> 00:53:17,565
All right, man.

799
00:53:19,867 --> 00:53:20,935
Let's get this over with.

800
00:53:29,209 --> 00:53:30,343
[man on phone] <i>Tick-tock.</i>

801
00:53:30,410 --> 00:53:33,648
<i>Tick-tock, tick-tock.</i>

802
00:53:35,348 --> 00:53:38,351
<i>Tick-tock, tick-tock.</i>

803
00:53:39,754 --> 00:53:41,923
[car horn blares]

804
00:54:06,313 --> 00:54:07,380
Gentlemen.

805
00:54:07,447 --> 00:54:09,316
-[car door closes]
-I'm Daniel.

806
00:54:10,785 --> 00:54:13,353
[timer ticking]

807
00:54:14,756 --> 00:54:15,823
Yeah, we know.

808
00:54:16,824 --> 00:54:17,759
What's next?

809
00:54:17,825 --> 00:54:18,760
[Daniel] We've got time.

810
00:54:19,259 --> 00:54:20,360
[One] For what?

811
00:54:20,995 --> 00:54:21,996
For killing time.

812
00:54:22,295 --> 00:54:24,431
["Welcome to Medina" plays]

813
00:54:36,944 --> 00:54:38,345
[Daniel] <i>Welcome to Medina.</i>

814
00:54:38,411 --> 00:54:39,981
[car horns honking]

815
00:54:44,685 --> 00:54:46,954
[Daniel] <i>Your Western Wiki</i>
<i>might describe this place</i>

816
00:54:47,021 --> 00:54:49,690
<i>as the ancient most</i>
<i>populous area of Dakar.</i>

817
00:54:55,495 --> 00:54:57,330
<i>The cultural center of the city.</i>

818
00:54:58,232 --> 00:55:00,001
["Welcome to Medina"
continues]

819
00:55:05,106 --> 00:55:06,373
[Daniel] <i>I call it home.</i>

820
00:55:28,129 --> 00:55:32,667
[cell phone chimes]

821
00:55:39,674 --> 00:55:41,876
Be on your best behavior, boys.

822
00:55:41,943 --> 00:55:44,679
People in this neighborhood
are very sensitive.

823
00:55:45,378 --> 00:55:46,514
Well, that's too bad.

824
00:55:46,581 --> 00:55:48,549
I was looking forward
to blowing something up.

825
00:55:50,151 --> 00:55:52,119
["Welcome to Medina"
continues]

826
00:55:58,391 --> 00:56:00,027
[kids yelling]

827
00:56:23,084 --> 00:56:24,685
[chimes]

828
00:56:30,191 --> 00:56:31,926
[chiming continues]

829
00:56:58,653 --> 00:56:59,921
[goat bleats in distance]

830
00:57:01,155 --> 00:57:02,422
[One] <i>So, where are you from?</i>

831
00:57:04,025 --> 00:57:05,526
[Daniel] <i>I'm from that place</i>
<i>that they signed</i>

832
00:57:05,593 --> 00:57:07,494
<i>the Declaration of</i>
<i>Independence.</i>

833
00:57:11,299 --> 00:57:12,600
<i>I used to teach history there.</i>

834
00:57:13,134 --> 00:57:13,935
<i>Now I live here.</i>

835
00:57:14,235 --> 00:57:15,336
[man 1 in Wolof]

836
00:57:15,403 --> 00:57:18,906
[in Wolof]

837
00:57:21,542 --> 00:57:22,543
[in English] May I?

838
00:57:24,412 --> 00:57:25,680
How do you know
the man on the phone?

839
00:57:28,149 --> 00:57:28,950
Wait here.

840
00:57:35,256 --> 00:57:36,456
[Daniel] Emmanuel!

841
00:57:38,893 --> 00:57:40,027
Look at you!

842
00:57:40,995 --> 00:57:42,029
You got big.

843
00:57:43,597 --> 00:57:46,200
You're all dressed up! Wow!

844
00:57:51,973 --> 00:57:53,541
Are you ready to go?

845
00:57:59,513 --> 00:58:01,115
Come on, come on.

846
00:58:01,182 --> 00:58:02,149
[bleats]

847
00:58:06,486 --> 00:58:08,055
[Two] Oh, fuck me.

848
00:58:08,589 --> 00:58:09,623
This is Emmanuel.

849
00:58:10,091 --> 00:58:11,993
You... you brought us here
for a fucking goat?

850
00:58:12,626 --> 00:58:13,928
He's not just any goat.

851
00:58:15,229 --> 00:58:16,897
-Take him.
-No.

852
00:58:19,100 --> 00:58:19,900
Take him.

853
00:58:22,336 --> 00:58:23,237
[sighs]

854
00:58:27,842 --> 00:58:29,643
Yeah, tie your hand around here.

855
00:58:30,411 --> 00:58:31,245
There you go.

856
00:58:32,113 --> 00:58:34,248
Hold his chin.
It makes him feel comfortable.

857
00:58:35,416 --> 00:58:37,118
[scoffs]

858
00:58:37,184 --> 00:58:38,986
That's right. Let's go.

859
00:58:40,388 --> 00:58:42,289
-[bleats]
-That's good shit. That's good.

860
00:58:43,824 --> 00:58:45,860
-[One] Okay, let's go, come on.
-[bleating continues]

861
00:58:45,926 --> 00:58:46,761
Let's go.

862
00:58:47,328 --> 00:58:48,462
Come on.

863
00:58:48,529 --> 00:58:51,265
Emmanuel is the most famous ram
in Senegal.

864
00:58:51,866 --> 00:58:54,001
He even has
his own social media following.

865
00:58:54,068 --> 00:58:56,103
[upbeat music]

866
00:59:08,549 --> 00:59:11,552
He's exceptional,
just like you guys.

867
00:59:12,019 --> 00:59:14,021
So we're all supposed
to go fuck a sheep now?

868
00:59:14,088 --> 00:59:16,690
No, no, no, no, no. There's no--
none of that here.

869
00:59:16,757 --> 00:59:18,259
I don't know where you're from.

870
00:59:18,325 --> 00:59:19,627
No, he's coming with us.

871
00:59:22,163 --> 00:59:22,963
Where?

872
00:59:24,231 --> 00:59:25,299
[Daniel] You'll find out.

873
00:59:25,666 --> 00:59:26,700
[Daniel in French]

874
00:59:26,767 --> 00:59:27,902
[One in English] Easy, easy.

875
00:59:28,436 --> 00:59:29,603
[Daniel in French]

876
00:59:29,737 --> 00:59:31,338
[in English]
Emmanuel, we'll be right back.

877
00:59:32,473 --> 00:59:33,607
[Emmanuel bleats]

878
00:59:34,241 --> 00:59:35,309
What are we doing here?

879
00:59:36,143 --> 00:59:37,278
We're getting you ready.

880
00:59:38,513 --> 00:59:39,914
Ready for what?

881
00:59:42,116 --> 00:59:42,983
For the party.

882
00:59:43,584 --> 00:59:45,719
[rock music plays]

883
00:59:57,566 --> 00:59:58,732
[Daniel in Wolof]

884
01:00:13,481 --> 01:00:14,715
[speaking Wolof]

885
01:00:24,593 --> 01:00:26,160
[in English] New outfits, huh?

886
01:00:27,728 --> 01:00:29,263
New mission, new chapter.

887
01:00:29,330 --> 01:00:31,398
[rock music continues]

888
01:01:06,467 --> 01:01:08,402
[rock music intensifies]

889
01:01:17,178 --> 01:01:18,045
Time's up.

890
01:01:19,180 --> 01:01:21,115
[discordant music]

891
01:01:33,494 --> 01:01:34,596
[Daniel]
So, what do you think, Emmanuel?

892
01:01:34,663 --> 01:01:35,763
[Emmanuel bleats]

893
01:01:35,829 --> 01:01:37,698
Do you think these boys
can walk the walk?

894
01:01:38,165 --> 01:01:38,899
[Emmanuel bleats]

895
01:01:38,966 --> 01:01:40,301
[Daniel]
Yeah, I know you're right.

896
01:01:41,670 --> 01:01:43,804
[Daniel] Wait until you see
the chip I got for you.

897
01:01:43,871 --> 01:01:45,039
You're a lucky fella.

898
01:01:46,641 --> 01:01:47,474
[Daniel] She's gonna love you.

899
01:01:48,175 --> 01:01:49,276
[Emmanuel bleats]

900
01:01:52,313 --> 01:01:53,180
[One] How do you know him?

901
01:01:53,981 --> 01:01:55,316
[Daniel]
We've actually never met.

902
01:01:56,651 --> 01:01:57,985
[text beeps]

903
01:01:58,687 --> 01:01:59,820
[One] Why trust him?

904
01:02:00,721 --> 01:02:02,456
[Daniel]
Trust has nothing to do with it.

905
01:02:03,123 --> 01:02:04,825
Listen, we're all born
with a ticking clock.

906
01:02:04,892 --> 01:02:05,926
The main thing is...

907
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:08,128
is that our death
serves a greater purpose.

908
01:02:08,195 --> 01:02:10,231
For many people here,
living can be

909
01:02:10,297 --> 01:02:11,932
more painful than dying.

910
01:02:13,234 --> 01:02:15,169
And what's this, uh...
greater purpose

911
01:02:15,236 --> 01:02:17,204
for all the people
that have died today?

912
01:02:22,076 --> 01:02:23,678
You think because
you saw a little death,

913
01:02:23,744 --> 01:02:26,013
it makes you all of a sudden
more righteous?

914
01:02:27,181 --> 01:02:28,082
Look around you.

915
01:02:29,350 --> 01:02:31,819
Look at the conditions
these people are living in.

916
01:02:35,624 --> 01:02:36,890
[Daniel] <i>No jobs,</i>

917
01:02:37,858 --> 01:02:39,026
<i>no money.</i>

918
01:02:41,462 --> 01:02:42,429
<i>They have nothing.</i>

919
01:02:43,464 --> 01:02:44,265
<i>Right?</i>

920
01:02:45,299 --> 01:02:47,334
<i>And you people call it</i>
<i>a third-world country</i>

921
01:02:47,401 --> 01:02:48,235
<i>so you can feel better</i>

922
01:02:48,302 --> 01:02:50,505
<i>about your own</i>
<i>standard of living.</i>

923
01:02:52,406 --> 01:02:54,975
<i>But look closer, my friends.</i>

924
01:02:56,310 --> 01:02:58,245
[pensive music]

925
01:03:03,484 --> 01:03:06,954
<i>This is a misery you created</i>
<i>and fed on for centuries</i>

926
01:03:07,021 --> 01:03:09,189
<i>and it won't save you</i>
<i>from the truth.</i>

927
01:03:10,891 --> 01:03:13,394
<i>The truth that these people</i>
<i>are the light.</i>

928
01:03:14,161 --> 01:03:15,796
<i>Because they don't need</i>
<i>your appetite</i>

929
01:03:15,863 --> 01:03:17,398
<i>for material wealth</i>

930
01:03:17,464 --> 01:03:20,067
<i>to understand</i>
<i>the meaning of happiness.</i>

931
01:03:27,274 --> 01:03:29,243
[Daniel] <i>You talk of people</i>
<i>dying, but, instead...</i>

932
01:03:29,711 --> 01:03:33,414
<i>think about how you should</i>
<i>start living, my brothers.</i>

933
01:03:40,755 --> 01:03:42,856
<i>From zero comes the one.</i>

934
01:03:43,792 --> 01:03:46,026
<i>From the one come the million.</i>

935
01:03:47,061 --> 01:03:49,564
<i>Rise and breathe, my friends.</i>

936
01:03:50,831 --> 01:03:52,299
<i>Rise and breathe.</i>

937
01:03:53,200 --> 01:03:56,571
<i>Because death isn't the end</i>
<i>when your life has meaning.</i>

938
01:03:58,138 --> 01:03:59,774
<i>What you're going to accomplish</i>

939
01:03:59,840 --> 01:04:01,776
<i>will start a fire so large</i>

940
01:04:01,842 --> 01:04:04,912
<i>it will shake the order</i>
<i>of things to come.</i>

941
01:04:05,446 --> 01:04:06,880
<i>And I couldn't be prouder</i>

942
01:04:06,947 --> 01:04:10,184
<i>to be by your side</i>
<i>when it happens.</i>

943
01:04:12,787 --> 01:04:13,588
Right?

944
01:04:22,429 --> 01:04:24,398
[knocks]

945
01:04:25,600 --> 01:04:26,967
[Two] The guy on the phone...

946
01:04:28,001 --> 01:04:28,902
What the hell
does he want with us?

947
01:04:28,969 --> 01:04:30,170
[Emmanuel bleats]

948
01:04:30,237 --> 01:04:31,872
[Daniel] He wants to release you
once you're done,

949
01:04:31,939 --> 01:04:33,307
just like he told you.

950
01:04:34,542 --> 01:04:35,342
[Emmanuel bleats]

951
01:04:36,343 --> 01:04:37,144
How do you know?

952
01:04:38,045 --> 01:04:39,913
Because I'm the one
that's gonna release you.

953
01:04:40,715 --> 01:04:41,949
After my wedding.

954
01:04:42,015 --> 01:04:43,350
-[Emmanuel bleats]
-[sighs]

955
01:04:43,417 --> 01:04:46,220
-Our mission is your wedding?
-Your mission comes after.

956
01:04:46,286 --> 01:04:50,023
For now, Emmanuel is my present
to my bride's family,

957
01:04:50,090 --> 01:04:51,225
and you're gonna be my
witnesses.

958
01:04:51,291 --> 01:04:53,528
-We're gonna be your what?
-[Emmanuel bleats]

959
01:04:54,495 --> 01:04:57,632
You're gonna play your part
when I handle my business.

960
01:04:58,465 --> 01:04:59,266
After...

961
01:05:00,568 --> 01:05:01,636
I'll set you free.

962
01:05:02,670 --> 01:05:03,605
[Emmanuel bleats]

963
01:05:04,405 --> 01:05:07,307
Now, would you please
stop strangling my ram?

964
01:05:10,010 --> 01:05:11,311
-Okay.
-[Daniel] Thank you.

965
01:05:11,912 --> 01:05:13,380
[bleats]

966
01:05:16,016 --> 01:05:17,519
-Mama!
-Daniel!

967
01:05:17,585 --> 01:05:18,820
[laughs]

968
01:05:18,887 --> 01:05:20,655
[Daniel]
<i>This is a private ceremony.</i>

969
01:05:20,722 --> 01:05:22,256
[imam speaks in Wolof]

970
01:05:22,322 --> 01:05:23,725
[Daniel in English]
<i>So, I would like you to behave</i>

971
01:05:23,792 --> 01:05:25,660
<i>in front of my bride's family.</i>

972
01:05:25,727 --> 01:05:28,195
[imam in Wolof]

973
01:05:44,144 --> 01:05:45,279
[in English]
What does that mean?

974
01:05:46,714 --> 01:05:49,450
[imam speaks in Wolof]

975
01:05:49,517 --> 01:05:51,285
[Ladja in English]
Well, thanks for being here.

976
01:05:51,985 --> 01:05:53,588
It's nice to meet
Daniel's friends.

977
01:05:54,121 --> 01:05:56,356
Did he tell you
that he's the only American

978
01:05:56,423 --> 01:05:58,893
to have obtained the right
to teach in a Koranic school?

979
01:05:59,761 --> 01:06:02,831
I even asked Daniel if he's
gonna take me to Philadelphia.

980
01:06:03,631 --> 01:06:06,166
Babe, you don't want to go
to America, believe me.

981
01:06:06,935 --> 01:06:08,402
No? Why's that?

982
01:06:09,436 --> 01:06:10,337
America?

983
01:06:11,138 --> 01:06:13,140
The place that only took
a few centuries

984
01:06:13,207 --> 01:06:16,143
to become worse than the empire
that spawned it?

985
01:06:16,210 --> 01:06:20,247
The place that exterminated
all the original inhabitants?

986
01:06:20,314 --> 01:06:23,718
The place that enslaved
the very people who built it?

987
01:06:25,352 --> 01:06:28,222
And like a plague
of hateful intentions,

988
01:06:28,288 --> 01:06:31,425
proceeds to destroy
and destabilize

989
01:06:31,492 --> 01:06:33,393
the rest of the world?

990
01:06:33,460 --> 01:06:34,729
This is your place?

991
01:06:35,930 --> 01:06:37,565
This is not a country.

992
01:06:39,466 --> 01:06:40,467
It's a disease.

993
01:06:41,168 --> 01:06:43,303
[suspenseful music]

994
01:06:47,307 --> 01:06:49,443
[Ladja] Well, now you understand

995
01:06:49,511 --> 01:06:51,445
why his previous school
fired him.

996
01:06:52,580 --> 01:06:55,315
Yeah, well,
I want to teach to enlighten

997
01:06:55,382 --> 01:06:58,485
and liberate, not to control.

998
01:07:00,387 --> 01:07:01,856
If you gentlemen
would excuse me,

999
01:07:01,923 --> 01:07:03,758
I have some business
to attend to.

1000
01:07:14,434 --> 01:07:15,235
[One] Cut it.

1001
01:07:18,673 --> 01:07:19,574
[One] Okay.

1002
01:07:23,477 --> 01:07:24,444
[sharp snip]

1003
01:07:26,548 --> 01:07:27,782
[chimes]

1004
01:07:30,552 --> 01:07:32,252
[ticking]

1005
01:07:39,894 --> 01:07:41,161
[cell phone rings, vibrates]

1006
01:07:44,498 --> 01:07:46,534
[man on phone]
<i>You've done very, very well.</i>

1007
01:07:47,100 --> 01:07:48,135
<i>Thank you.</i>

1008
01:07:49,136 --> 01:07:50,404
<i>Last mission.</i>

1009
01:07:51,873 --> 01:07:53,273
<i>Follow Daniel...</i>

1010
01:07:53,741 --> 01:07:54,542
